{title: Come, Thou Fount of Every Blessing}
{lyricist: Robert Robinson, 1758}
{composer: NETTLETON, Wyeth's Repository of Sacred Music, 1813}
{copyright: Public domain}
{key: D}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 96}

{start_of_verse}
[D]Come, Thou Fount of [G]every [D]blessing,
[D]Tune my heart to [A]sing Thy [D]grace;
[D]Streams of mercy, [G]never [D]ceasing,
[D]Call for songs of [A]loudest [D]praise.
[D]Teach me some me[A]lodious [Bm]sonnet,
[G]Sung by flaming [D]tongues a[A]bove;
[D]Praise the mount! I'm [G]fixed up[D]on it,
[D]Mount of Thy re[A]deeming [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[D]Here I raise my [G]Eben[D]ezer;
[D]Hither by Thy [A]help I'm [D]come;
[D]And I hope, by [G]Thy good [D]pleasure,
[D]Safely to ar[A]rive at [D]home.
[D]Jesus sought me [A]when a [Bm]stranger,
[G]Wandering from the [D]fold of [A]God;
[D]He, to rescue [G]me from [D]danger,
[D]Interposed His [A]precious [D]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[D]O to grace how [G]great a [D]debtor
[D]Daily I'm con[A]strained to [D]be!
[D]Let Thy goodness, [G]like a [D]fetter,
[D]Bind my wandering [A]heart to [D]Thee.
[D]Prone to wander, [A]Lord, I [Bm]feel it,
[G]Prone to leave the [D]God I [A]love;
[D]Here's my heart, O [G]take and [D]seal it,
[D]Seal it for Thy [A]courts a[D]bove.
{end_of_verse}
